ETE invoke a non-callable handler and reject outside Express 4 error handling. Describe default Node process-failure inference with the gateway-token prerequisite, not a tested crash.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"path\": \"service/routes.mjs\",\n          \"quote\": \"const sessions = {};\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"service/routes.mjs\",\n          \"quote\": \"const session = sessions[req.headers['mcp-session-id']];\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"service/routes.mjs\",\n          \"quote\": \"await session.handleRequest(req, res);\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"guards\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"auth_boundary\",\n      \"description\": \"Gateway auth precedes all MCP handlers. No unauthenticated/default-public attack claim and no invented OAuth audience gap.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"path\": \"service/routes.mjs\",\n          \"quote\": \"app.use('/mcp',\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"runtime_scope\",\n      \"description\": \"No runtime test, measured crash, deployed secret or host-audit claim. External controls require evidence.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"path\": \"README.md\",\n          \"quote\": \"Host audit, framing limits, ingress policy and process supervision require host evidence.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"coverage\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"coverage_get\",\n      \"description\": \"Assess GET session lookup and error handling, not just file presence.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"path\": \"service/routes.mjs\",\n          \"quote\": \"app.get('/mcp',\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"coverage_delete\",\n      \"description\": \"Assess DELETE lookup and error handling separately or explicitly verify equivalent enforcement.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"path\": \"service/routes.mjs\",\n          \"quote\": \"app.delete('/mcp',\"\n        }\n     